Pandas & NumPy
Learn:
import pandas as pd
import numpy as np
Then load a CSV:
df = pd.read_csv("students.csv")
print(df.head())
print(df.shape)
print(df.columns)
print(df.info())
#Data Cleaning & Analysis
print(df.isnull().sum())
Remove missing values:
df = df.dropna()


Calculate averages:
print("Average Math:", df["Math"].mean())print("Average Physics:", df["Physics"].mean())


Find the highest marks:
print(df["Math"].max())


You can also use NumPy:
average = np.mean(df["Math"])print(average)
Visualization with Matplotlib
Learn the three required chart types.
Bar chart
import matplotlib.pyplot as pltplt.bar(df["Name"], df["Math"])plt.xlabel("Student")plt.ylabel("Math Marks")plt.title("Math Marks by Student")plt.show()


Line chart
plt.plot(df["Name"], df["Math"], marker="o")plt.xlabel("Student")plt.ylabel("Marks")plt.title("Student Math Performance")plt.show()


Pie chart
plt.pie(    df["Math"],    labels=df["Name"],    autopct="%1.1f%%")plt.title("Math Marks Distribution")plt.show()
